llowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T03:08:40Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T05:47:44Z","body":"I think the simplest way to fix this issue would be to just check if the number ends with a .0 and if so remove it. I just added a few lines to EditorPerformanceProfiler::_create_label which do this:\n\n```\ndefault: {\n\tString ret = TS->format_number(rtos(p_value));\n\tif (ret.ends_with(\".0\")) {\n\t\tret = ret.pad_decimals(0);\n\t}\n\treturn ret;\n}\n```\n\nThis fixes the issue of integers as floats in the Monitor:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/84ed5db2-3bbe-4122-a0ed-21bf1a0051bf)\n\nBy the way, I don't see how it's a flaw that get_monitor() returns a double. In 4.3 it returned a double but we didn't see the trailing \".0\". Anyway, I'll probably create a pull request for this in a bit.\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495773709/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495889131","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99577#issuecomment-2495889131","issue_url":"https://a